    <scope doc="This module provides primitive operations to write multi-threaded programs. The &apos;threading&apos; module provides a more convenient interface." ilk="blob" lang="Python" name="thread">
      <scope classrefs="object" doc="A lock object is a synchronization primitive.  To create a lock, call the PyThread_allocate_lock() function.  Methods are:  acquire() -- lock the lock, possibly blocking until it can be obtained release() -- unlock of the lock locked() -- test whether the lock is currently locked  A lock is not owned by the thread that locked it; another thread may unlock it.  A thread attempting to lock a lock that it has already locked will block until another thread unlocks it.  Deadlocks may ensue." ilk="class" name="LockType" />
