      <scope classrefs="DistutilsError" doc="Syntactic/semantic errors in command options, such as use of mutually conflicting options, or inconsistent options, badly-spelled values, etc.  No distinction is made between option values originating in the setup script, the command line, config files, or what-have-you -- but if we *know* something originated in the setup script, we&apos;ll raise DistutilsSetupError instead." ilk="class" name="DistutilsOptionError" />
      <scope classrefs="DistutilsError" doc="We don&apos;t know how to do something on the current platform (but we do know how to do it on some platform) -- eg. trying to compile C files on a platform not supported by a CCompiler subclass." ilk="class" name="DistutilsPlatformError" />
