      <scope classrefs="FormContentDict" doc="Form content as dictionary expecting a single value per field. If you only expect a single value for each field, then form[key] will return that single value.  It will raise an IndexError if that expectation is not true.  If you expect a field to have possible multiple values, than you can use form.getlist(key) to get all of the values.  values() and items() are a compromise: they return single strings where there is a single value, and lists of strings otherwise." ilk="class" line="815" lineend="846" name="SvFormContentDict">
