      <scope classrefs="BaseCookie" doc="SmartCookie SmartCookie supports arbitrary objects as cookie values.  If the object is a string, then it is quoted.  If the object is not a string, however, then SmartCookie will use cPickle to serialize the object into a string representation.  Note: Large cookie values add overhead because they must be retransmitted on every HTTP transaction.  Note: HTTP has a 2k limit on the size of a cookie.  This class does not check for this limit, so be careful!!!" ilk="class" line="695" lineend="723" name="SmartCookie">
