    <scope doc="plistlib.py -- a tool to generate and parse MacOSX .plist files. The PropertList (.plist) file format is a simple XML pickle supporting basic object types, like dictionaries, lists, numbers and strings. Usually the top level object is a dictionary.  To write out a plist file, use the writePlist(rootObject, pathOrFile) function. &apos;rootObject&apos; is the top level object, &apos;pathOrFile&apos; is a filename or a (writable) file object.  To parse a plist from a file, use the readPlist(pathOrFile) function, with a file name or a (readable) file object as the only argument. It" ilk="blob" lang="Python" name="plistlib">
